{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 8.889,
   "text": "Three kids got the same thousand dollars, in the S and P five hundred, on the same day, and twenty years later, one had over ten times as much."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 9.038,
   "end": 11.293,
   "text": "Wait, how? It's the same money!"
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 11.442,
   "end": 16.34,
   "text": "That's tiny pieces of five hundred big companies, all bought at the start of two thousand six."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 16.44,
   "end": 22.374,
   "text": "Then came the two thousand eight crash, and by year-end, each thousand was worth about seven hundred seventy."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 22.474,
   "end": 26.179,
   "text": "Kid one sells at year-end and hides the cash in a shoebox."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 26.278,
   "end": 32.446,
   "text": "Kid two sells too, but buys back at the end of two thousand nine, after missing a twenty-six percent rebound."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 32.546,
   "end": 34.412,
   "text": "Kid three does nothing at all."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 34.809,
   "end": 38.852,
   "text": "At first, kid one feels smart, because shoebox money can't crash."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-09",
   "start": 39.189,
   "end": 47.431,
   "text": "By the end of twenty twenty-five, kid one has seven hundred seventy, kid two about sixty-four hundred, and kid three about eight thousand."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-10",
   "start": 47.53,
   "end": 51.365,
   "text": "Same money, same day, and the kid who did nothing won."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-11",
   "start": 51.703,
   "end": 55.565,
   "text": "So if your money crashed, would you sell, wait or hold?"
  }
